SARU 26.10

SARU 26.10 makes key-use prompts more informative by identifying the
application from which an SSH agent request originated, adds full support
for high-DPI displays and makes the agent considerably more reliable.

What is new

  * Key confirmation and selection windows can now show which application
    originated a request, even when it reaches SARU through an intermediary
    such as Windows OpenSSH, the Windows command processor or PuTTY Plink.
    SARU follows the process hierarchy and skips known intermediary executables;
    the default list is detected from installed SSH clients and can be reviewed
    or changed in the notification settings.  Originating-process information
    can also be disabled there.

  * Windows, icons and the tray menu scale correctly on high-DPI displays,
    including setups with several monitors using different scaling.

  * SARU no longer closes unexpectedly when an SSH client disconnects while a
    confirmation or key selection window is open; such windows are now closed
    automatically.

  * The agent keeps running after errors caused by a single client and
    recovers its Windows SSH agent and Hyper-V listeners, for example after
    resume from sleep.

  * Long replies to Hyper-V virtual machines are no longer truncated.

  * The Pageant compatibility option in the settings now takes effect.

  * Agent protocol handling follows RFC 9987, and destination-restricted keys
    are checked the same way as in OpenSSH.

  * Several smaller fixes in the settings, dialogs, the Hyper-V helper and the
    WSL bridge.
